<title>JAPAN: Oyo Corp falls sharply on poor earnings.</title>
<headline>Oyo Corp falls sharply on poor earnings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Oyo Corp fell sharply on the Tokyo Stock Exchange early on Tuesday morning on its poor interim parent earnings announced on Monday, traders said.</p>
<p>Shares of the geological research firm fell 190 yen, or 4.90 percent, to 3,690 by 0047 GMT.</p>
<p>It was the third-largest percentage loser on the first section of the TSE.  </p>
<p>Oyo said on Monday it posted a parent curret profit of 2.78 billion yen in the six months to June 30, 1997, against 3.59 billion yen in the same period a year ago.</p>
<p>- Tokyo equities desk (813) 3432-9404</p>
